From e40795011a17182132cdc3e89715b0348b864ef8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeoDeadware <351117497+LeoDeadware@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:21:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/24] Mac: native render scale, 16:10 crop present, race HUD
 moved into the visible corners

- nv2a_metal: render scale follows the drawable (h/480, 1..4x) unless the
  option/RECOMP_GL_SCALE set it; square pixels per axis; NV2A 1/16 px snap
  ported to MSL (u_snap_y)
- present: on a screen narrower than 16:9 fill the height and cut the sides
  (NFSU2_SCREEN=fit letterbox, =fill stretch)
- hud_wide.c: race HUD elements (touching sprites, previous frame) wholly
  left/right of the middle move inward by (1 - visible); NFSU2_HUD_WIDE=0 off
- NFSU2_WINDOW=WxH for windowed dev runs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
